    "Recall that squaring means multiplying a number by itself.",
    "Use the anchor 50² = 2500 to derive nearby squares quickly.",
    "Apply (50+d)² = (25+d)|d² and (50−d)² = (25−d)|d².",
    "Use squares in area and cricket average problems."
  ],
  "coreIdeas": [
    "50 is the anchor — 50² = 2500.",
    "For numbers above 50: add d to 25 for left, d² for right.",
    "For numbers below 50: subtract d from 25 for left, d² for right.",
    "Right part must always be 2 digits — pad with zero if needed."
  ],
